    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a pivotal Sunday slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leading the charge at a commanding 81.21 efficiency score. Facing J. Lopez, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.67 xERA matchup and positive park factors, making him the anchor of today\u2019s offense. Joining him in the tier of \"Strong\" starts, **Jackson Merrill** (70.50) is a critical component given his speed profile. We have specifically weighted **Jackson Merrill** higher due to the opposing starter's slow delivery, which provides a tangible boost to his stolen base upside\u2014a priority for the Waves given our league-wide scarcity strategy. Both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (65.79 and 65.57, respectively) remain locked into the lineup against the vulnerable arm of Cantillo, with park conditions providing a significant 16% lift to their base projections.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Kyle Tucker** (55.52), who narrowly landed in the \"Marginal\" category. While **Kyle Tucker** possesses an elite pedigree, the matchup against Ch. Burns (3.44 xERA) tempers his expected output, limiting his ceiling relative to our other outfield options. Our bench remains heavily compromised by the injury bug, with **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** all confirmed on the IL, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is unavailable due to a team off-day. Consequently, **Drake Baldwin** (48.10) and **Wade Meckler** (51.27) round out the daily starting unit by default; while these scores reflect a lack of elite alternatives, we are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** closely. Should any last-minute defensive substitutions occur, we will be forced to rotate in reserves like **Jacob Wilson** or **Heliot Ramos**, though current projections suggest sticking to the stated lineup to protect our remaining game caps.",
